Q1. Write a C program that demonstrates the use of buffer blocks, use fixed-size buffers to store,
    display and clear the buffer block. Display cleared buffer block.

#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main()
{
    char buffer[20] = "Operating System";

    printf("Buffer block: %s\n", buffer);

    memset(buffer, 0, sizeof(buffer));

    printf("Cleared buffer block: %s\n", buffer);

    return 0;
}
